lse,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2025-07-21T01:44:56Z","updated_at":"2025-09-22T12:07:12Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot v4.5.beta (71a994815)\n\n### System information\n\nArch Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Thu, 19 Jun 2025 14:41:19 +0000 on Tty - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NV134 - AMD Ryzen 7 5800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.21 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe operators `and` and `or` can take any operand types. However, constant evaluation will give an error if both types aren't one of `bool`, `int`, `float`, `null`, or `Object`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t# constant eval\n\tprint(42 and \"hello\") # Error: Invalid operands to operator or, int and String\n\t\n\t# runtime typed eval\n\tvar a := 42\n\tvar b := \"hello\"\n\tprint(a and b) # prints \"true\"\n\t\n\t# runtime untyped eval\n\tvar ua = 42\n\tvar ub = \"hello\"\n\tprint(ua and ub) # prints \"true\"\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108813/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108813/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}